<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.developer.applesignin</key>
	<array>
		<string>Default</string>
	</array>
	<key>com.apple.developer.in-app-payments</key>
	<array>
		<string>merchant.com.mailrooms.app</string>
	</array>
	<!--
		Universal Links — v0.7.0.26 enabled against mailroomclub.vercel.app.

		AASA file is live at
		  https://mailroomclub.vercel.app/.well-known/apple-app-site-association
		(verified 200 + application/json on 2026-05-15). Pattern: any URL
		matching /claim* routes here.

		On iOS 14+ with the Mailroom app installed, tapping a claim link
		from iMessage / Mail / Safari opens the app via expo-router's
		deep link handler. Without the app installed, the App Clip
		(com.mailrooms.app.Clip) presents the address form natively
		without an install. Without iOS at all (Android, desktop), the
		static HTML page at claim/index.html serves as fallback.

		Apple Developer Portal step required before this builds clean:
		https://developer.apple.com/account → Identifiers →
		com.mailrooms.app → Associated Domains capability → check.
		(One-time, takes effect on next provisioning profile refresh
		which Xcode handles automatically.)
	-->
	<key>com.apple.developer.associated-domains</key>
	<array>
		<string>applinks:mailroomclub.vercel.app</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
